os-pangolin is a native FreeBSD/OPNsense integration for Pangolin.

It provides:

  - a Pangolin machine client with a native FreeBSD tun(4), ioctl(2) and
    route(8) network backend;
  - a Newt-compatible site connector (the upstream Pangolin CLI embeds Newt
    with `pangolin up site`);
  - a native subnet router that lets selected local VLANs reach remote
    Pangolin resources through the firewall, without a client on the LAN
    device and without Linux containers, VMs or compatibility layers;
  - OPNsense-owned pf anchors with source-scoped NAT/filter rules, automatic
    route lifecycle and fail-closed cleanup;
  - an os-pangolin-owned Unbound include file for private resource aliases,
    with conflict detection against manually managed entries;
  - CARP active/passive gating for HA deployments.

The agent is built from the official fosrl/newt and fosrl/olm sources with a
small, documented FreeBSD port. See the project repository for the exact
upstream commits, patch files and security model.
